        "problem": "Compute $\\text{E}[\\frac{2}{3}X]$ if $\\text{E}[X]=3.$",
        "worked_solution": "For any constant $a$ and any random variable $X,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[aX]=a\\text{E}[X].\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[\\frac{2}{3}X] & =\\frac{2}{3}\\text{E}[X] \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}(3) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
